/-!
# The quadric cone: sharpness of the dimension bound for the local Picard group

[Stacks, Tag 0F2J] is the example showing that the dimension bound of
[Stacks, Tag 0F2I] is sharp.  For a field `k` the three-dimensional complete local
hypersurface
`A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)`
is a Noetherian local complete intersection of dimension exactly three, and the Picard
group of its punctured spectrum `U = Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` is nontrivial.  The witness is the ideal
`I = (x,z)`, which cuts out an effective Cartier divisor `D` on `U`; since
`A/I` has depth at least one and `I` has depth at least two, `I = Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))`, so a
trivialization of `𝒪_U(-D)` would make `I` isomorphic to `Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = A` — impossible,
because `I` is not generated by one element.

## Main definitions

* `hypersurface` is `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)`, the variables indexed by `Fin 4` in the
  order `x,y,z,w`.
* `coordinateIdeal` is the ideal `I = (x,z)` of `A`.
* `cartierDivisor` is the restriction to the punctured spectrum
  `Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum A` of the closed subscheme of `Spec A` cut out by `I`.

## Main results

* `dimension_bound_isSharp`: **[Stacks, Tag 0F2J]** — for every field `k` the ring
  `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is a Noetherian local complete intersection of dimension
  exactly three, so it satisfies every hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0F2I] except
  `dim A ≥ 4`, and the Picard group of its punctured spectrum is nontrivial.
* `hypersurface_isLocalRing`, `hypersurface_isNoetherianRing`,
  `hypersurface_isCompleteIntersectionRing` and `hypersurface_krullDim` are its first four
  conjuncts.
* `picardGroup_not_subsingleton'` is the last one: `Pic(U)` is nontrivial, stated at
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.picardGroup`, the same Picard group [Stacks, Tag 0F2I] is
  stated at, so it is literally the negation of that proposition's conclusion for this `A`.
* `negativeTwist_not_trivial'`: `𝒪_U(-D)` is not a trivial invertible `𝒪_U`-module.
* `picardGroup_not_subsingleton` and `negativeTwist_not_trivial` are those two statements with
  assertions about `U` taken as hypotheses: that `A → Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` is bijective and that
  `I ≅ Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))` as `A`-modules, and for the first also that `I` cuts out an effective
  Cartier divisor `D` on `U`.
* `coordinateIdeal_not_principal`: `I` is not generated by a single element.
* `quotient_depth`: `depth(A/I) = 2`, so in particular at least one.
* `coordinateIdeal_depth`: `depth(I) = 3`, so in particular at least two.

## Implementation notes

**Charts.**  The `i`-th chart is `puncturedChart k i = ι ⁻¹ᵁ D(x_i)`, affine because `D(x_i)`
is affine and contained in `U`.  Its ring of sections is `Γ(Spec A, ι ''ᵁ V_i)` by
definition of an open subscheme, and the ideal of `D` there is computed by
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`, which keeps both opens as they are written and so
needs no transport along `ι ''ᵁ ι ⁻¹ᵁ D(x_i) = D(x_i)`.  That equality is used only once,
in `chartTransport`, to move to the spelling at which `Γ(Spec A, D(x_i))` is the
localization `A_{x_i}`.

**Spellings.**  The variables are indexed by `Fin 4`, in the order `x,y,z,w`.
`cartierDivisor` is the scheme-theoretic restriction to `U` of the ideal sheaf of `I` on the
ambient affine scheme.  `sectionsAsModuleFunctor` reads the global sections of a sheaf of
`𝒪_U`-modules as an `A`-module along `sectionsAsModuleRingMap`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F2J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F2J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F2I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F2I)
-/


@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters
open scoped Pointwise

namespace Stacks.PuncturedSpectrumPicard.QuadricCone

universe u

/-- The four-variable formal power series ring over the coefficient field. -/
public abbrev powerSeriesRing (k : Type u) [Field k] := MvPowerSeries (Fin 4) k

/-- The determinant equation defining the hypersurface. -/
public abbrev equation (k : Type u) [Field k] : powerSeriesRing k :=
  MvPowerSeries.X 0 * MvPowerSeries.X 1 - MvPowerSeries.X 2 * MvPowerSeries.X 3

/-- The complete local hypersurface cut out by the determinant equation. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "the hypersurface"]
public abbrev hypersurface (k : Type u) [Field k] :=
  powerSeriesRing k ⧸ Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set (powerSeriesRing k))

/-- The image of a coordinate power series in the hypersurface quotient. -/
public abbrev coordinate (k : Type u) [Field k] (i : Fin 4) : hypersurface k :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPowerSeries.X i)

/-- The ideal generated by the first and third coordinates. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "the ideal (x,z)"]
public abbrev coordinateIdeal (k : Type u) [Field k] : Ideal (hypersurface k) :=
  Ideal.span ({coordinate k 0, coordinate k 2} : Set (hypersurface k))

private theorem equation_ne_zero (k : Type u) [Field k] : equation k ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  let α : Fin 4 →₀ ℕ := Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1
  have hc := congrArg (MvPowerSeries.coeff α) h
  have hc' : MvPowerSeries.coeff α (equation k) = 1 := by
    simp [equation, α, MvPowerSeries.X_def, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial_mul]
  rw [hc'] at hc
  exact one_ne_zero hc

/-- The equation `xy - zw` lies in the maximal ideal of `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧`. -/
private theorem equation_mem_maximalIdeal (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    equation k ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (powerSeriesRing k) := by
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff, MvPowerSeries.isUnit_iff_constantCoeff]
  simp [equation]

/-- The ideal generated by the equation is proper. -/
private theorem span_equation_ne_top (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set (powerSeriesRing k)) ≠ ⊤ :=
  ne_top_of_le_ne_top (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).ne_top
    (Ideal.span_le.2 (by simpa using equation_mem_maximalIdeal k))

/-- The equation is a nonzerodivisor of `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧`. -/
private theorem equation_isSMulRegular (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsSMulRegular (powerSeriesRing k) (equation k) :=
  IsSMulRegular.of_right_eq_zero_of_smul fun _ hx =>
    (mul_eq_zero.mp hx).resolve_left (equation_ne_zero k)

/-- The maximal ideal of `k⟦x_1, …, x_n⟧` is generated by the variables. -/
private theorem mvPowerSeries_maximalIdeal_eq_span_X (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ) :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)) :=
  MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X k n


/-- The maximal ideal of `k⟦x_1, …, x_n⟧` is generated by `n` elements. -/
private theorem mvPowerSeries_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ) :
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)).spanFinrank ≤ n := by
  rw [MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X]
  refine (Submodule.spanFinrank_span_le_ncard_of_finite (Set.finite_range _)).trans ?_
  simpa [← Set.image_univ] using
    Set.ncard_image_le (f := (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
      Set.finite_univ

private theorem mvPowerSeries_fin_krullDim (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ) :
    ringKrullDim (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) = n := by
  classical
  have hupper : ringKrullDim (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) ≤ (n : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    (ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal _).trans
      (by exact_mod_cast mvPowerSeries_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le k n)
  have hlower : ∀ m : ℕ, (m : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim (MvPowerSeries (Fin m) k) := by
    intro m
    induction m with
    | zero => exact ringKrullDim_nonneg_of_nontrivial
    | succ m ih =>
      rw [ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv (MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv k m).toRingEquiv]
      calc
        ((m + 1 : ℕ) : WithBot ℕ∞) = (m : WithBot ℕ∞) + 1 := by simp
        _ ≤ ringKrullDim (MvPowerSeries (Fin m) k) + 1 := add_le_add ih le_rfl
        _ ≤ ringKrullDim (PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin m) k)) :=
          ringKrullDim_succ_le_ringKrullDim_powerseries
  exact le_antisymm hupper (hlower n)

/-- The power series ring `k⟦x_1, …, x_n⟧` is a regular local ring. -/
private theorem mvPowerSeries_isRegularLocalRing (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ)
    [IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)] :
    IsRegularLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) := by
  apply IsRegularLocalRing.of_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le
  have h : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)).spanFinrank ≤
      (n : WithBot ℕ∞) := by exact_mod_cast mvPowerSeries_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal_le k n
  simpa [mvPowerSeries_fin_krullDim] using h

/-- The power series ring `k⟦x_1, …, x_n⟧` has depth `n`. -/
private theorem mvPowerSeries_depth (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ)
    [IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)] :
    Module.depth (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) = n := by
  have := mvPowerSeries_isRegularLocalRing k n
  have h := (IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
    (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k)).2
  change (Module.depth _ _ _ : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim _ at h
  rw [mvPowerSeries_fin_krullDim] at h
  exact WithBot.coe_injective h

/-- The ring `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is a local ring. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "local ring", instance]
public theorem hypersurface_isLocalRing (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsLocalRing (hypersurface k) := by
  let : Nontrivial (powerSeriesRing k ⧸ Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set (powerSeriesRing k))) :=
    Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr (span_equation_ne_top k)
  exact .of_surjective' _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- The ring `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is Noetherian. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "Noetherian ring", instance]
public theorem hypersurface_isNoetherianRing (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsNoetherianRing (hypersurface k) := by
  let : IsNoetherianRing (powerSeriesRing k) :=
    mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing k 4
  infer_instance


/-- The ring map `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw) ⟶ k⟦u,v⟧` substituting `a j` for the `j`-th coordinate,
for substitutions with `a 0 * a 1 = a 2 * a 3`. -/
private noncomputable def hypersurface_substHom (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (a : Fin 4 → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (ha : MvPowerSeries.HasSubst a)
    (hrel : a 0 * a 1 = a 2 * a 3) : hypersurface k →+* MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ (MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom ha).toRingHom (by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp hx
    have hf : MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom ha (equation k) = 0 := by
      rw [MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom_apply, equation, MvPowerSeries.subst_sub ha,
        MvPowerSeries.subst_mul ha, MvPowerSeries.subst_mul ha, MvPowerSeries.subst_X ha,
        MvPowerSeries.subst_X ha, MvPowerSeries.subst_X ha, MvPowerSeries.subst_X ha, hrel,
        sub_self]
    simp [map_mul, hf])

private theorem hypersurface_substHom_coordinate (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (a : Fin 4 → MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k) (ha : MvPowerSeries.HasSubst a)
    (hrel : a 0 * a 1 = a 2 * a 3) (j : Fin 4) :
    hypersurface_substHom k a ha hrel (coordinate k j) = a j := by
  simp [hypersurface_substHom, coordinate, MvPowerSeries.substAlgHom_apply,
    MvPowerSeries.subst_X ha]

private noncomputable def hypersurface_to_twoVariable (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    hypersurface k →+* MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
  hypersurface_substHom k
    (fun j => if j = 0 then MvPowerSeries.X 0 else if j = 2 then MvPowerSeries.X 1 else 0)
    (MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero fun j => by split_ifs <;> simp) (by simp)

private theorem hypersurface_to_twoVariable_coordinate (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (j : Fin 4) :
    hypersurface_to_twoVariable k (coordinate k j) =
      if j = 0 then MvPowerSeries.X 0 else if j = 2 then MvPowerSeries.X 1 else 0 :=
  hypersurface_substHom_coordinate k _ _ _ j

private noncomputable def coordinateQuotient_ringEquiv (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) ≃+* MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k := by
  classical
  let B := powerSeriesRing k
  let q : Ideal B := Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)
  let J : Ideal B := Ideal.span ({MvPowerSeries.X 0, MvPowerSeries.X 2} : Set B)
  have hcoords : coordinateIdeal k = Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk q) J := by
    change Ideal.span ({coordinate k 0, coordinate k 2} : Set (hypersurface k)) = _
    rw [Ideal.map_span]
    congr 1
    ext z
    simp [coordinate, q]
    rfl
  have hqJ : q ≤ J := by
    apply Ideal.span_le.2
    intro f hf
    rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hf
    subst f
    rw [equation]
    apply sub_mem
    · exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ J (Ideal.subset_span (by simp))
    · exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ J (Ideal.subset_span (by simp))
  have hsup : q ⊔ J = J := sup_eq_right.mpr hqJ
  let e0 : (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) ≃+*
      ((hypersurface k) ⧸ Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk q) J) :=
    Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hcoords
  let e1 : ((hypersurface k) ⧸ Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk q) J) ≃+*
      (B ⧸ q ⊔ J) := DoubleQuot.quotQuotEquivQuotSup q J
  let e2 : (B ⧸ q ⊔ J) ≃+* (B ⧸ J) := Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hsup
  let p : Fin 4 ≃ Fin 4 := Equiv.swap 1 2
  let g : B ≃ₐ[k] B := MvPowerSeries.renameEquiv k p
  let K : Ideal B := Ideal.span
      (Set.range (fun i : Fin 2 =>
        (MvPowerSeries.X (Fin.castLE (by omega) i) : B)))
  have hK : K = Ideal.map (g : B →+* B) J := by
    change Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i : Fin 2 =>
      (MvPowerSeries.X (Fin.castLE (by omega) i) : B))) =
        Ideal.map (g : B →+* B)
          (Ideal.span ({MvPowerSeries.X 0, MvPowerSeries.X 2} : Set B))
    rw [Ideal.map_span]
    congr 1
    ext z
    have h0 : g (MvPowerSeries.X 0 : B) = MvPowerSeries.X 0 := by
      change MvPowerSeries.rename p (MvPowerSeries.X 0) = MvPowerSeries.X 0
      rw [MvPowerSeries.rename_X]
      rw [Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne (by decide) (by decide)]
    have h2 : g (MvPowerSeries.X 2 : B) = MvPowerSeries.X 1 := by
      change MvPowerSeries.rename p (MvPowerSeries.X 2) = MvPowerSeries.X 1
      rw [MvPowerSeries.rename_X]
      rw [Equiv.swap_apply_right]
    simp [h0, h2, eq_comm]
  let e3 : (B ⧸ J) ≃ₐ[k] (B ⧸ K) := Ideal.quotientEquivAlg J K g hK
  let e4 := Classical.choice (quotient_initial_vars
    (R := k) (n := 4) (r := 2) (by omega))
  exact e0.trans (e1.trans (e2.trans (e3.toRingEquiv.trans e4.toRingEquiv)))


/-- The self-depth of a local ring along its maximal ideal is invariant under a ring
isomorphism. -/
private alias depth_self_eq_of_ringEquiv := Module.depth_self_eq_of_ringEquiv


private theorem isAdicComplete_quotient_local
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    [IsPrecomplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R]
    (I : Ideal R) [IsLocalRing (R ⧸ I)] :
    IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (R ⧸ I)) (R ⧸ I) := by
  let m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R
  have hpre : IsPrecomplete m (R ⧸ I) := by
    apply AdicCompletion.of_surjective_iff.mp
    intro z
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := AdicCompletion.map_surjective m
      (f := I.mkQ) I.mkQ_surjective z
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := AdicCompletion.of_surjective m R y
    refine ⟨I.mkQ x, ?_⟩
    rw [← AdicCompletion.map_of, hx, hy]
  have hpre' : IsPrecomplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (R ⧸ I)) (R ⧸ I) := by
    rw [← IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
      Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective]
    exact IsPrecomplete.map_algebraMap_iff.mpr hpre
  let : IsPrecomplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (R ⧸ I)) (R ⧸ I) := hpre'
  let : IsHausdorff (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (R ⧸ I)) (R ⧸ I) :=
    IsHausdorff.of_le_jacobson _ _ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_le_jacobson ⊥)
  exact ⟨⟩

private theorem hypersurface_isAdicComplete (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k)) (hypersurface k) := by
  let B := powerSeriesRing k
  let I : Ideal B := Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)
  let : IsLocalRing B := inferInstance
  let : IsNoetherianRing B := mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing k 4
  let : IsLocalRing (B ⧸ I) := hypersurface_isLocalRing k
  have hcomp : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B := by
    rw [MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X]
    infer_instance
  let : IsPrecomplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B := hcomp.toIsPrecomplete
  exact isAdicComplete_quotient_local I

/-- The ring `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is a complete intersection ring. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "complete intersection"]
public theorem hypersurface_isCompleteIntersectionRing (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    LocalCompleteIntersection.IsCompleteIntersectionRing (hypersurface k) := by
  classical
  let B := powerSeriesRing k
  let A := hypersurface k
  let I : Ideal B := Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)
  let : IsNoetherianRing B := mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing k 4
  let : IsLocalRing A := hypersurface_isLocalRing k
  let : Nontrivial A := inferInstance
  let hcomplete := hypersurface_isAdicComplete k
  let : IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A := hcomplete
  let e : A ≃+* AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A :=
    (AdicCompletion.ofAlgEquiv (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)).toRingEquiv
  let : Nontrivial (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) :=
    e.injective.nontrivial
  let : IsLocalRing (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A) :=
    IsLocalRing.of_surjective' e.toRingHom e.surjective
  let : IsRegularLocalRing B := mvPowerSeries_isRegularLocalRing k 4
  have hproper : I ≠ ⊤ := span_equation_ne_top k
  let : Nontrivial (B ⧸ I) := Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hproper
  let : Nontrivial (QuotSMulTop (equation k) B) := by
    rw [QuotSMulTop, Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff]
    intro htop
    have hmem : (1 : B) ∈ (equation k) • (⊤ : Submodule B B) := by
      rw [htop]
      simp
    rw [Submodule.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists] at hmem
    obtain ⟨b, -, hb⟩ := hmem
    exact hproper (Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top.mpr
      (IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one b (by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hb)))
  have hseq : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular B [equation k] :=
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.cons (equation_isSMulRegular k)
      (RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular.nil B (QuotSMulTop (equation k) B))
  let f : B →+* AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A :=
    e.toRingHom.comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)
  have hf : Function.Surjective f := e.surjective.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  let : IsLocalHom f := IsLocalHom.of_surjective f hf
  have hker : RingHom.ker f = Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B) := by
    rw [RingHom.ker_comp_of_injective _ e.injective]
    ext x
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  refine ⟨B, inferInstance, inferInstance, f, hf, inferInstance, ?_⟩
  refine ⟨[equation k], hseq, ?_⟩
  simpa [Ideal.ofList] using hker.symm

/-- The restriction of the closed subscheme cut out by the coordinate ideal
to the punctured spectrum. -/
public abbrev cartierDivisor (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.IdealSheafData :=
  (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (X := Spec (.of (hypersurface k)))
    ((coordinateIdeal k).map ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (hypersurface k))).inv).hom)).comap
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι

/-- The ring `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` has Krull dimension three. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "dimension three"]
public theorem hypersurface_krullDim (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    ringKrullDim (hypersurface k) = 3 := by
  let B := powerSeriesRing k
  have hquot :=
    ringKrullDim_quotient_span_singleton_succ_eq_ringKrullDim_of_mem_nonZeroDivisors
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero (equation_ne_zero k)) (equation_mem_maximalIdeal k)
  rw [mvPowerSeries_fin_krullDim] at hquot
  change ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)) + 1 = 4 at hquot
  show ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)) = 3
  cases hdim : ringKrullDim (B ⧸ Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set B)) with
  | bot =>
    rw [hdim] at hquot
    simp at hquot
  | coe d =>
    cases d with
    | top =>
      rw [hdim, ← WithBot.coe_one, ← WithBot.coe_add] at hquot
      exact (ENat.top_ne_natCast 4 (WithBot.coe_injective hquot)).elim
    | coe d =>
      rw [hdim, ← WithBot.coe_one, ← WithBot.coe_add] at hquot
      change (↑((↑d : ℕ∞) + 1) : WithBot ℕ∞) =
        (↑(4 : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) at hquot
      have hEnat : (↑d : ℕ∞) + 1 = 4 := WithBot.coe_injective hquot
      have h' := hEnat
      rw [← ENat.natCast_one, ← ENat.natCast_add] at h'
      have hnat : d + 1 = 4 := ENat.natCast_inj.mp h'
      have : d = 3 := by omega
      simp [this]

private lemma mvPowerSeries_X_prime (k : Type u) [Field k] (n : ℕ) (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    Prime (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin (n + 1)) k) := by
  let : IsDomain (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) := NoZeroDivisors.to_isDomain _
  let e := (MvPowerSeries.renameEquiv k (Equiv.swap i 0)).trans
    (MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv k n)
  apply (MulEquiv.prime_iff e).mp
  have he : e (MvPowerSeries.X i) = PowerSeries.X := by
    show MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv k n
      (MvPowerSeries.rename (Equiv.swap i 0) (MvPowerSeries.X i)) = _
    rw [MvPowerSeries.rename_X, Equiv.swap_apply_left, MvPowerSeries.finSuccEquiv_X_zero]
  rw [he]
  exact PowerSeries.X_prime

private lemma regular_quotient_of_prime_not_dvd {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R]
    {p f : R} (hp : Prime p) (hpf : ¬ p ∣ f) :
    IsRegular (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) p) := by
  rw [isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors, mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff]
  have h (a : R ⧸ Ideal.span {f})
      (ha : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {f}) p * a = 0) : a = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
    rw [← map_mul, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at ha
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ha
    have hpc : p ∣ c := (hp.dvd_mul.mp (hc ▸ dvd_mul_right p b)).resolve_left hpf
    obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := hpc
    have hb : b = f * d := by
      apply mul_left_cancel₀ hp.ne_zero
      rw [hc]
      ring
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    exact ⟨d, hb⟩
  exact ⟨h, fun a ha => h a (by simpa only [mul_comm] using ha)⟩

private lemma coordinate_regular (k : Type u) [Field k] (i : Fin 4)
    (hi : i = 0 ∨ i = 2) :
    IsRegular (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {equation k}) (MvPowerSeries.X i)) := by
  let : IsDomain (MvPowerSeries (Fin 4) k) := NoZeroDivisors.to_isDomain _
  apply regular_quotient_of_prime_not_dvd (mvPowerSeries_X_prime k 3 i)
  intro h
  rw [MvPowerSeries.X_dvd_iff] at h
  rcases hi with rfl | rfl
  · have hc := h (Finsupp.single 2 1 + Finsupp.single 3 1) (by simp)
    have he : MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 2 1 + Finsupp.single 3 1)
        (equation k) = -1 := by
      simp [equation, MvPowerSeries.X_def, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial_mul]
    rw [he] at hc
    exact neg_ne_zero.mpr one_ne_zero hc
  · have hc := h (Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1) (by simp)
    have he : MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single 0 1 + Finsupp.single 1 1)
        (equation k) = 1 := by
      simp [equation, MvPowerSeries.X_def, MvPowerSeries.coeff_monomial_mul]
    rw [he] at hc
    exact one_ne_zero hc

private lemma exists_regular_generator_of_relation {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (x y z w : R) (hrel : x * y = z * w) (hx : IsRegular x) (hz : IsRegular z)
    (hu : IsUnit x ∨ IsUnit y ∨ IsUnit z ∨ IsUnit w) :
    ∃ t : R, IsRegular t ∧ Ideal.span ({x, z} : Set R) = Ideal.span {t} := by
  rcases hu with hu | hu | hu | hu
  · refine ⟨1, isRegular_one, ?_⟩
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_one]
    exact Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)) hu
  · refine ⟨z, hz, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
    · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
      simp only [Set.insert_subset_iff, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe,
        Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
      exact ⟨hu.dvd_mul_right.mp (hrel.symm ▸ dvd_mul_right z w), dvd_refl _⟩
    · exact Ideal.span_mono (by simp)
  · refine ⟨1, isRegular_one, ?_⟩
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_one]
    exact Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ (Ideal.subset_span (by simp)) hu
  · refine ⟨x, hx, le_antisymm ?_ ?_⟩
    · apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
      simp only [Set.insert_subset_iff, Set.singleton_subset_iff, SetLike.mem_coe,
        Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
      exact ⟨dvd_refl _, hu.dvd_mul_right.mp (hrel ▸ dvd_mul_right x y)⟩
    · exact Ideal.span_mono (by simp)

private lemma hypersurface_maximalIdeal_eq_span_coordinates (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k) = Ideal.span (Set.range (coordinate k)) := by
  have h := IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set (powerSeriesRing k))))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  rw [MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp] at h
  exact h.symm

/-- The ideal `(x,z)` of `k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is not generated by a single element. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "nonprincipal ideal"]
public theorem coordinateIdeal_not_principal (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    ¬ ∃ a : hypersurface k, coordinateIdeal k = Ideal.span ({a} : Set (hypersurface k)) :=
  by
    classical
    let C := MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k
    let φ := hypersurface_to_twoVariable k
    have hvars : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C) =
        Ideal.span ({MvPowerSeries.X 0, MvPowerSeries.X 1} : Set C) := by
      rw [MvPowerSeries.maximalIdeal_eq_span_range_X]
      congr 1
      ext z
      simp only [Set.mem_range, Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩
        fin_cases i <;> simp
      · rintro (rfl | rfl)
        · exact ⟨0, rfl⟩
        · exact ⟨1, rfl⟩
    intro hprincipal
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hprincipal
    have hmap : Ideal.map φ (coordinateIdeal k) =
        Ideal.span ({MvPowerSeries.X 0, MvPowerSeries.X 1} : Set C) := by
      rw [coordinateIdeal, Ideal.map_span]
      congr 1
      ext z
      simp [φ, hypersurface_to_twoVariable_coordinate]
    have hmapped : Ideal.map φ (coordinateIdeal k) = Ideal.span ({φ a} : Set C) := by
      rw [ha, Ideal.map_span]
      simp
      rfl
    have hmax : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C = Ideal.span ({φ a} : Set C) :=
      hvars.trans (hmap.symm.trans hmapped)
    have hgens : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal C).spanFinrank ≤ 1 := by
      rw [hmax]
      refine (Submodule.spanFinrank_span_le_ncard_of_finite (Set.finite_singleton (φ a))).trans ?_
      simp
    have hdim : ringKrullDim C ≤ (1 : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
      (ringKrullDim_le_spanFinrank_maximalIdeal C).trans (by exact_mod_cast hgens)
    rw [mvPowerSeries_fin_krullDim k 2] at hdim
    norm_num at hdim

/-- The quotient of `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` by the ideal `(x,z)` has depth two as an
`A`-module, along the maximal ideal of `A`. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "quotient depth"]
public theorem quotient_depth (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    Module.depth (hypersurface k) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k))
      (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) = 2 := by
  classical
  let A := hypersurface k
  let Q := A ⧸ coordinateIdeal k
  let C := MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k
  let e := coordinateQuotient_ringEquiv k
  let : Nontrivial Q := e.symm.injective.nontrivial
  let : IsLocalRing Q := IsLocalRing.of_surjective' (e.symm : C →+* Q) e.symm.surjective
  let : IsNoetherianRing C := mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing k 2
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective
      (algebraMap (hypersurface k) (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) :
        hypersurface k →+* (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k)) := by
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hdepthQ : Module.depth (hypersurface k)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k))
      (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) =
      Module.depth (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k)
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k))
        (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k) := by
    rw [Module.depth_eq_depth_map_algebraMap (B := Q) hsurj,
      IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective
        (algebraMap (hypersurface k) (hypersurface k ⧸ coordinateIdeal k)) hsurj]
  rw [hdepthQ, Module.depth_self_eq_of_ringEquiv e]
  exact mvPowerSeries_depth k 2

private lemma hypersurface_depth (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    Module.depth (hypersurface k) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k))
      (hypersurface k) = 3 := by
  classical
  let B := powerSeriesRing k
  let A := hypersurface k
  let m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B
  let : IsNoetherianRing B := mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing k 4
  have hdepth : Module.depth B m B = 4 := mvPowerSeries_depth k 4
  let e : QuotSMulTop (equation k) B ≃ₗ[B] A := by
    apply Submodule.quotEquivOfEq
    ext a
    simp only [Submodule.mem_smul_pointwise_iff_exists, Submodule.mem_top, true_and,
      smul_eq_mul, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    constructor <;> rintro ⟨b, hb⟩ <;> exact ⟨b, by simpa [mul_comm] using hb.symm⟩
  have hd := (Module.depth_quotSMulTop_succ_eq_depth_and_exists_isRegular_append m B).1
    (equation k) (equation_mem_maximalIdeal k) (equation_isSMulRegular k)
  rw [Module.depth_eq_depth_of_linearEquiv m e, hdepth] at hd
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (algebraMap B A) := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  rw [Module.depth_eq_depth_map_algebraMap hsurj,
    IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective _ hsurj] at hd
  apply ENat.add_left_injective_of_ne_top (n := 1) (by simp)
  convert hd using 1
  norm_num

/-- The ideal `(x,z)` of `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` has depth three as an `A`-module, along
the maximal ideal of `A`. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "ideal depth"]
public theorem coordinateIdeal_depth (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    Module.depth (hypersurface k) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k))
      (coordinateIdeal k) = 3 := by
  have h := Module.min_depth_le_depth_of_exact
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k))
    (LinearMap.exact_subtype_mkQ (coordinateIdeal k))
    (coordinateIdeal k).subtype_injective (coordinateIdeal k).mkQ_surjective
  rw [hypersurface_depth k, quotient_depth k] at h
  have hlow : 3 ≤ Module.depth (hypersurface k)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k)) (coordinateIdeal k) := by
    have hh := h.2.2
    norm_num at hh
    exact hh
  have hu : Module.depth (hypersurface k)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k)) (coordinateIdeal k) - 1 ≤ 2 :=
    (min_le_iff.mp h.2.1).resolve_left (by norm_num)
  apply le_antisymm _ hlow
  calc
    _ = (_ - 1) + 1 := (tsub_add_cancel_of_le
      (le_trans (by norm_num : (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ 3) hlow)).symm
    _ ≤ 2 + 1 := add_le_add hu le_rfl
    _ = 3 := by norm_num

/-! ### The conclusion of Stacks 0F2J -/

attribute [local implicit_reducible]
  TopCat.Sheaf
  CategoryTheory.sheafCompose

/-- The canonical ring map `A ⟶ Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` from `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` to the global
functions on its punctured spectrum. -/
public abbrev sectionsAsModuleRingMap (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    hypersurface k →+*
      Γ((Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme, ⊤) :=
  ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (hypersurface k))).inv ≫
    (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι.appTop).hom

/-- Global sections over the punctured spectrum of a sheaf of `𝒪_U`-modules, read as an
`A`-module along `sectionsAsModuleRingMap`. -/
public abbrev sectionsAsModuleFunctor (k : Type u) [Field k] :=
  _root_.SheafOfModules.evaluation
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.ringCatSheaf (op ⊤) ⋙
    ModuleCat.restrictScalars (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k)

/-! ### Charts of the punctured spectrum -/

section Inputs

variable (k : Type u) [Field k]

/-- `Spec A` for the hypersurface `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)`. -/
private abbrev ambient : Scheme.{u} := Spec (CommRingCat.of (hypersurface k))

/-- The canonical isomorphism from `A` to the global functions on `Spec A`. -/
private abbrev toGamma : hypersurface k →+* Γ(ambient k, ⊤) :=
  ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (hypersurface k))).inv).hom

/-- The basic open `D(x_i) ⊆ Spec A` of the `i`-th coordinate. -/
private abbrev chart (i : Fin 4) : (ambient k).Opens :=
  (ambient k).basicOpen (toGamma k (coordinate k i))

private lemma coordinate_mem_maximalIdeal (i : Fin 4) :
    coordinate k i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (hypersurface k) := by
  rw [hypersurface_maximalIdeal_eq_span_coordinates]
  exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

private lemma chart_eq (i : Fin 4) :
    chart k i = PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen (coordinate k i) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine (R := CommRingCat.of (hypersurface k))
    (coordinate k i)

private lemma chart_le_puncturedSpectrum (i : Fin 4) :
    chart k i ≤ Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k) := by
  rw [chart_eq]
  exact Stacks.Divisors.basicOpen_le_puncturedSpectrum (coordinate_mem_maximalIdeal k i)

private lemma isAffineOpen_chart (i : Fin 4) : IsAffineOpen (chart k i) :=
  (isAffineOpen_top (ambient k)).basicOpen _

/-- The `i`-th chart of the punctured spectrum: the preimage of `D(x_i)`. -/
private abbrev puncturedChart (i : Fin 4) :
    (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.Opens :=
  (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ⁻¹ᵁ chart k i

private lemma isAffineOpen_puncturedChart (i : Fin 4) :
    IsAffineOpen (puncturedChart k i) :=
  (isAffineOpen_chart k i).preimage_of_isOpenImmersion _
    (by simpa using chart_le_puncturedSpectrum k i)

/-- Every point of the punctured spectrum avoids one of the four coordinates. -/
private lemma puncturedSpectrum_le_iSup_chart :
    Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k) ≤ ⨆ i : Fin 4, chart k i := by
  intro p hp
  have hex : ∃ i : Fin 4, coordinate k i ∉ (p : PrimeSpectrum (hypersurface k)).asIdeal := by
    obtain ⟨g, hgm, hgp⟩ :=
      Stacks.Divisors.exists_mem_maximalIdeal_notMem_of_mem_puncturedSpectrum
        (A := hypersurface k) (p := p) hp
    by_contra hcon
    simp only [not_exists, not_not] at hcon
    rw [hypersurface_maximalIdeal_eq_span_coordinates] at hgm
    exact hgp ((Ideal.span_le.2 (by rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact hcon i)) hgm)
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hex
  refine TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨i, ?_⟩
  rw [chart_eq]
  exact hi

/-- The four charts cover the punctured spectrum. -/
private lemma puncturedChart_covers :
    (⊤ : (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.Opens) ≤
      ⨆ i : Fin 4, puncturedChart k i := by
  intro x _
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1
    (puncturedSpectrum_le_iSup_chart k x.2)
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨i, hi⟩

/-! ### Global functions on the punctured spectrum -/

/-- **`Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = A`.**  The depth of `A` along its maximal ideal is `3`, so the restriction
map on global functions to the punctured spectrum is bijective. -/
private lemma bijective_sectionsAsModuleRingMap :
    Function.Bijective (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k) := by
  refine Stacks.LocalCohomology.bijective_appTop_of_punctured_of_depth_ge_two
    (hypersurface k) (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ?_ ?_
  · rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    rfl
  · rw [hypersurface_depth k]
    norm_num

/-! ### The ideal of the divisor on a chart -/

/-- The composite `A ⟶ Γ(U, V_i)` restricting a function on `Spec A` to the `i`-th chart.
The target is spelled on the ambient scheme; `Γ(U, V) = Γ(Spec A, ι ''ᵁ V)` by definition. -/
private abbrev chartSection (i : Fin 4) :
    hypersurface k →+* Γ(ambient k,
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ puncturedChart k i) :=
  (((ambient k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top :
    (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ
      puncturedChart k i ≤ ⊤)).op).hom).comp (toGamma k)

private lemma cartierDivisor_ideal_puncturedChart (i : Fin 4) :
    (cartierDivisor k).ideal ⟨puncturedChart k i, isAffineOpen_puncturedChart k i⟩ =
      Ideal.map (chartSection k i) (coordinateIdeal k) := by
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE _ _ ⟨chart k i, isAffineOpen_chart k i⟩
      ⟨puncturedChart k i, isAffineOpen_puncturedChart k i⟩ le_rfl,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map]
  congr 1

/-! ### The divisor is an effective Cartier divisor -/

private lemma isRegular_ringEquiv {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (e : R ≃+* S)
    {a : R} (ha : IsRegular a) : IsRegular (e a) := by
  have key : ∀ x y : S, e a * x = e a * y → x = y := by
    intro x y hxy
    have h : a * e.symm x = a * e.symm y := by
      apply e.injective
      simp only [map_mul, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
      exact hxy
    simpa using congrArg e (ha.left h)
  exact ⟨fun x y hxy => key x y hxy,
    fun x y hxy => key x y (by simpa only [mul_comm] using hxy)⟩

/-- The canonical isomorphism `A ≃+* Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`. -/
private abbrev gammaRingEquiv : hypersurface k ≃+* Γ(ambient k, ⊤) :=
  (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of (hypersurface k))).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

private lemma isRegular_chartSection (i : Fin 4) {j : Fin 4} (hj : j = 0 ∨ j = 2) :
    IsRegular (chartSection k i (coordinate k j)) := by
  have h0 : toGamma k (coordinate k j) ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(ambient k, ⊤) := by
    rw [← isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors]
    exact isRegular_ringEquiv (gammaRingEquiv k) (coordinate_regular k j hj)
  rw [isRegular_iff_mem_nonZeroDivisors]
  exact Stacks.Divisors.mem_nonZeroDivisors_res (isAffineOpen_top (ambient k)) h0 le_top

private lemma isUnit_chartSection_self (i : Fin 4) :
    IsUnit (chartSection k i (coordinate k i)) := by
  have h1 : IsUnit (((ambient k).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE ((ambient k).basicOpen_le (toGamma k (coordinate k i)))).op).hom
        (toGamma k (coordinate k i))) :=
    (ambient k).toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen (toGamma k (coordinate k i))
  have h2 := h1.map (((ambient k).presheaf.map
    (homOfLE ((Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι.image_preimage_le
      (chart k i))).op).hom)
  have hcomp : ((ambient k).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE ((Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι.image_preimage_le
        (chart k i))).op).hom
        ((((ambient k).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE ((ambient k).basicOpen_le (toGamma k (coordinate k i)))).op).hom)
            (toGamma k (coordinate k i))) = chartSection k i (coordinate k i) := by
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
    rfl
  rw [← hcomp]
  exact h2

private lemma chartSection_relation (i : Fin 4) :
    chartSection k i (coordinate k 0) * chartSection k i (coordinate k 1) =
      chartSection k i (coordinate k 2) * chartSection k i (coordinate k 3) := by
  have hrel : coordinate k 0 * coordinate k 1 = coordinate k 2 * coordinate k 3 := by
    have hz : (Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (Ideal.span ({equation k} : Set (powerSeriesRing k)))) (equation k) = 0 :=
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
    rw [equation, map_sub, map_mul, map_mul, sub_eq_zero] at hz
    exact hz
  simpa only [map_mul] using congrArg (chartSection k i) hrel

private lemma isUnit_chartSection_or (i : Fin 4) :
    IsUnit (chartSection k i (coordinate k 0)) ∨ IsUnit (chartSection k i (coordinate k 1)) ∨
      IsUnit (chartSection k i (coordinate k 2)) ∨
        IsUnit (chartSection k i (coordinate k 3)) := by
  have h := isUnit_chartSection_self k i
  fin_cases i
  · exact Or.inl h
  · exact Or.inr (Or.inl h)
  · exact Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inl h))
  · exact Or.inr (Or.inr (Or.inr h))

/-- The generator of `I = (x,z)` on the `i`-th chart, together with its regularity. -/
private lemma exists_regular_generator_chart (i : Fin 4) :
    ∃ t : Γ(ambient k, (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ
        puncturedChart k i),
      IsRegular t ∧ Ideal.map (chartSection k i) (coordinateIdeal k) = Ideal.span {t} := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hspan⟩ := exists_regular_generator_of_relation
    (chartSection k i (coordinate k 0)) (chartSection k i (coordinate k 1))
    (chartSection k i (coordinate k 2)) (chartSection k i (coordinate k 3))
    (chartSection_relation k i)
    (isRegular_chartSection k i (Or.inl rfl)) (isRegular_chartSection k i (Or.inr rfl))
    (isUnit_chartSection_or k i)
  refine ⟨t, ht, ?_⟩
  rw [coordinateIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_insert_eq, Set.image_singleton]
  exact hspan

/-- **`I = (x,z)` cuts out an effective Cartier divisor on the punctured spectrum.**  On the
chart `D(x)` the section `x` is a unit, so the ideal is the unit ideal; on `D(y)` the relation
`xy = zw` gives `x = zw/y`, so the ideal is `(z)` and `z` is a nonzerodivisor; and
symmetrically on `D(z)` and `D(w)`. -/
private lemma isEffectiveCartierDivisor_cartierDivisor :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (cartierDivisor k) := by
  refine Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_affineOpen _ fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 (puncturedChart_covers k (x := x) trivial)
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hspan⟩ := exists_regular_generator_chart k i
  exact ⟨puncturedChart k i, isAffineOpen_puncturedChart k i, hi, t, ht,
    (cartierDivisor_ideal_puncturedChart k i).trans hspan⟩


/-! ### The quotient `A/I` sees `y` -/

/-- The retraction `A ⟶ k⟦y, w⟧` killing `x` and `z`: substituting `x, z ↦ 0`,
`y ↦ u`, `w ↦ v`, which kills `xy - zw`. -/
private noncomputable def toComplementaryPair (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    hypersurface k →+* MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) k :=
  hypersurface_substHom k
    (fun j => if j = 1 then MvPowerSeries.X 0 else if j = 3 then MvPowerSeries.X 1 else 0)
    (MvPowerSeries.hasSubst_of_constantCoeff_zero fun j => by split_ifs <;> simp) (by simp)

private theorem toComplementaryPair_coordinate (k : Type u) [Field k] (j : Fin 4) :
    toComplementaryPair k (coordinate k j) =
      if j = 1 then MvPowerSeries.X 0 else if j = 3 then MvPowerSeries.X 1 else 0 :=
  hypersurface_substHom_coordinate k _ _ _ j

private lemma mvPowerSeries_X_ne_zero (n : ℕ) (i : Fin n) :
    (MvPowerSeries.X i : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) k) ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  have hc := congrArg (MvPowerSeries.coeff (Finsupp.single i 1)) h
  simp [MvPowerSeries.coeff_X] at hc

/-- `y` is not in `I = (x, z)`: the retraction above sends `x` and `z` to zero but `y` to a
nonzero power series. -/
private lemma coordinate_one_notMem_coordinateIdeal :
    coordinate k 1 ∉ coordinateIdeal k := by
  have hker : coordinateIdeal k ≤ RingHom.ker (toComplementaryPair k) := by
    refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
    intro z hz
    simp only [Set.mem_insert_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hz
    rcases hz with rfl | rfl
    · simp [RingHom.mem_ker, toComplementaryPair_coordinate]
    · simp [RingHom.mem_ker, toComplementaryPair_coordinate]
  intro hmem
  have h := hker hmem
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker, toComplementaryPair_coordinate] at h
  simp only [if_pos] at h
  exact mvPowerSeries_X_ne_zero k 2 0 h

/-- **`A/I` has no `y`-torsion.**  `A/I ≅ k⟦y, w⟧` is a domain in which `y` is nonzero, so a
power of `y` never annihilates a nonzero class. -/
private lemma mem_coordinateIdeal_of_pow_mul (n : ℕ) (a : hypersurface k)
    (h : coordinate k 1 ^ n * a ∈ coordinateIdeal k) : a ∈ coordinateIdeal k := by
  classical
  set e := coordinateQuotient_ringEquiv k with he
  have hz : e (Ideal.Quotient.mk (coordinateIdeal k) (coordinate k 1 ^ n * a)) = 0 := by
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 h, map_zero]
  rw [map_mul, map_mul, map_pow, map_pow] at hz
  have hne : e (Ideal.Quotient.mk (coordinateIdeal k) (coordinate k 1)) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    exact coordinate_one_notMem_coordinateIdeal k
      (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 (e.injective (by rw [h0, map_zero])))
  have hzero := (mul_eq_zero.1 hz).resolve_left (pow_ne_zero n hne)
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.1 (e.injective (by rw [hzero, map_zero]))


/-! ### From a chart back to `A` -/

private lemma mem_map_ringEquiv {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] (e : R ≃+* S)
    (J : Ideal R) (x : R) :
    (e : R →+* S) x ∈ Ideal.map (e : R →+* S) J ↔ x ∈ J := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun h => Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ h⟩
  have hcomp : ((e.symm : S →+* R).comp (e : R →+* S)) = RingHom.id R :=
    RingHom.ext fun y => e.symm_apply_apply y
  have hmap : Ideal.map (e.symm : S →+* R) (Ideal.map (e : R →+* S) J) = J := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map, hcomp, Ideal.map_id]
  have h2 := Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (e.symm : S →+* R) h
  rw [hmap] at h2
  have hx : (e.symm : S →+* R) ((e : R →+* S) x) = x := e.symm_apply_apply x
  rwa [hx] at h2

private lemma image_puncturedChart (i : Fin 4) :
    (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ puncturedChart k i =
      chart k i := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.image_preimage_eq_opensRange_inf, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
  exact inf_eq_right.mpr (chart_le_puncturedSpectrum k i)

/-- The restriction `A ⟶ Γ(Spec A, D(x_i))`, spelled at the basic open itself. -/
private abbrev chartSectionAmbient (i : Fin 4) : hypersurface k →+* Γ(ambient k, chart k i) :=
  (((ambient k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : chart k i ≤ ⊤)).op).hom).comp (toGamma k)

/-- The two spellings of the `i`-th chart differ by the equality `ι ''ᵁ V_i = D(x_i)`. -/
private abbrev chartTransport (i : Fin 4) :
    Γ(ambient k, (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ
        puncturedChart k i) ≃+* Γ(ambient k, chart k i) :=
  ((ambient k).presheaf.mapIso
    (eqToIso (image_puncturedChart k i).symm).op).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

private lemma chartTransport_chartSection (i : Fin 4) (a : hypersurface k) :
    (chartTransport k i : _ →+* _) (chartSection k i a) = chartSectionAmbient k i a := by
  show ((ambient k).presheaf.map (eqToHom (image_puncturedChart k i).symm).op).hom
      ((((ambient k).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top :
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).ι ''ᵁ
          puncturedChart k i ≤ ⊤)).op).hom) (toGamma k a)) = _
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

private lemma mem_map_chartSection_iff (i : Fin 4) (a : hypersurface k) :
    chartSection k i a ∈ Ideal.map (chartSection k i) (coordinateIdeal k) ↔
      chartSectionAmbient k i a ∈
        Ideal.map (chartSectionAmbient k i) (coordinateIdeal k) := by
  have hcomp : ((chartTransport k i : _ →+* _).comp (chartSection k i)) =
      chartSectionAmbient k i :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => chartTransport_chartSection k i x
  have key := mem_map_ringEquiv (chartTransport k i)
    (Ideal.map (chartSection k i) (coordinateIdeal k)) (chartSection k i a)
  rw [Ideal.map_map, hcomp, chartTransport_chartSection] at key
  exact key.symm

/-- A section of `A` lying in `I` on the chart `D(x_i)` is annihilated by a power of `x_i`
modulo `I`:  `Γ(Spec A, D(x_i))` is the localization of `A` at `x_i`. -/
private lemma exists_pow_mul_mem_of_mem_map_chartSectionAmbient (i : Fin 4)
    (a : hypersurface k)
    (h : chartSectionAmbient k i a ∈
      Ideal.map (chartSectionAmbient k i) (coordinateIdeal k)) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, coordinate k i ^ n * a ∈ coordinateIdeal k := by
  have hmapeq : Ideal.map (chartSectionAmbient k i) (coordinateIdeal k) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap Γ(ambient k, ⊤) Γ(ambient k, chart k i))
        (Ideal.map (toGamma k) (coordinateIdeal k)) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map]
    rfl
  have hval : chartSectionAmbient k i a =
      algebraMap Γ(ambient k, ⊤) Γ(ambient k, chart k i) (toGamma k a) := rfl
  rw [hmapeq, hval] at h
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hmem⟩ :=
    (IsLocalization.algebraMap_mem_map_algebraMap_iff
      (M := Submonoid.powers (toGamma k (coordinate k i)))
      (S := Γ(ambient k, chart k i)) _ _).mp h
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := hm
  refine ⟨n, ?_⟩
  rw [← mem_map_ringEquiv (gammaRingEquiv k) (coordinateIdeal k)]
  show toGamma k (coordinate k i ^ n * a) ∈ _
  rw [map_mul, map_pow]
  exact hmem


/-! ### The sections of the ideal sheaf over the punctured spectrum -/

/-- **Being annihilated by a closed immersion is a local condition.**  The structure sheaf of
the closed subscheme is a sheaf, so a section whose restrictions to a cover are annihilated is
annihilated. -/
private lemma subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_forall {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    {ι' : Type*} (V : ι' → X.Opens) (W : X.Opens) (hle : ∀ i, V i ≤ W)
    (hcover : W ≤ ⨆ i, V i) {r : Γ(X, W)}
    (h : ∀ i, I.subschemeι.app (V i) ((X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hle i)).op).hom r) = 0) :
    I.subschemeι.app W r = 0 := by
  refine Stacks.Divisors.eq_of_locally_eq (X := I.subscheme)
    (fun i => I.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ V i) (I.subschemeι ⁻¹ᵁ W)
    (fun i => (TopologicalSpace.Opens.map I.subschemeι.base).map (homOfLE (hle i))) ?_ _ 0 ?_
  · intro z hz
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 (hcover hz)
    exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨i, hi⟩
  · intro i
    rw [map_zero]
    have hnat := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (I.subschemeι.naturality (homOfLE (hle i)).op) r
    rw [CommRingCat.comp_apply, CommRingCat.comp_apply, Quiver.Hom.unop_op] at hnat
    rw [← hnat]
    exact h i

private lemma res_sectionsAsModuleRingMap (i : Fin 4) (a : hypersurface k) :
    ((Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (le_top : puncturedChart k i ≤ ⊤)).op).hom
      (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k a) = chartSection k i a := rfl

/-- **`I = Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))`.**  A global function on the punctured spectrum lies in the ideal
sheaf of `D` exactly when the corresponding element of `A` lies in `I = (x, z)`. -/
private lemma subschemeι_app_top_eq_zero_iff (a : hypersurface k) :
    (cartierDivisor k).subschemeι.app ⊤ (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k a) = 0 ↔
      a ∈ coordinateIdeal k := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h1 := Stacks.Divisors.subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_le (cartierDivisor k)
      (le_top : puncturedChart k 1 ≤ ⊤) h
    rw [res_sectionsAsModuleRingMap] at h1
    have h2 : chartSection k 1 a ∈ Ideal.map (chartSection k 1) (coordinateIdeal k) := by
      rw [← cartierDivisor_ideal_puncturedChart, ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app]
      exact h1
    rw [mem_map_chartSection_iff] at h2
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_pow_mul_mem_of_mem_map_chartSectionAmbient k 1 a h2
    exact mem_coordinateIdeal_of_pow_mul k n a hn
  · intro ha
    refine subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_forall (cartierDivisor k) (puncturedChart k) ⊤
      (fun _ => le_top) (puncturedChart_covers k) fun i => ?_
    rw [res_sectionsAsModuleRingMap]
    have h3 : chartSection k i a ∈ Ideal.map (chartSection k i) (coordinateIdeal k) :=
      Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha
    rw [← cartierDivisor_ideal_puncturedChart,
      ← Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app] at h3
    exact h3


/-! ### `I` as the module of sections of `𝒪_U(-D)` -/

/-- **`I ≅ Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))` as `A`-modules.**  The sections of the ideal sheaf over the
punctured spectrum are the functions on `U` annihilated by the closed immersion, and those are
exactly the elements of `I` under `Γ(U, 𝒪_U) = A`. -/
private lemma nonempty_coordinateIdeal_linearEquiv :
    Nonempty (coordinateIdeal k ≃ₗ[hypersurface k]
      (sectionsAsModuleFunctor k).obj
        (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k))) := by
  classical
  set D := cartierDivisor k with hD
  set ev := sectionsAsModuleFunctor k with hev
  let eK : ev.obj (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' D) ≅
      ev.obj (Stacks.Divisors.kernelIdealSheaf D) :=
    ev.mapIso (Stacks.Divisors.kernelIdealSheafIso D)
  let f : coordinateIdeal k →ₗ[hypersurface k]
      ev.obj (Stacks.Divisors.kernelIdealSheaf D) :=
    { toFun := fun x => Stacks.Divisors.mkKernelSection D (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k x.1)
        (by
          rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
          exact (subschemeι_app_top_eq_zero_iff k x.1).2 x.2)
      map_add' := fun x y => by
        refine Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection_injective D ?_
        show sectionsAsModuleRingMap k (x.1 + y.1) = _
        rw [map_add]
        rfl
      map_smul' := fun c x => by
        refine Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection_injective D ?_
        have h := Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection_smul D (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k c)
          (Stacks.Divisors.mkKernelSection D (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k x.1)
            (by
              rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
              exact (subschemeι_app_top_eq_zero_iff k x.1).2 x.2))
        show sectionsAsModuleRingMap k (c * x.1) = _
        rw [map_mul]
        exact h.symm }
  have hinj : Function.Injective f := fun x y hxy =>
    Subtype.ext ((bijective_sectionsAsModuleRingMap k).injective
      (congrArg (Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection D) hxy))
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective f := by
    intro z
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := (bijective_sectionsAsModuleRingMap k).surjective
      (Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection D z)
    have hmem : a ∈ coordinateIdeal k := by
      rw [← subschemeι_app_top_eq_zero_iff, ha]
      exact Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection_mem D z
    refine ⟨⟨a, hmem⟩, Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection_injective D ?_⟩
    show sectionsAsModuleRingMap k a = Stacks.Divisors.kernelSection D z
    exact ha
  exact ⟨(LinearEquiv.ofBijective f ⟨hinj, hsurj⟩).trans eK.toLinearEquiv.symm⟩


end Inputs

/-! ### The conclusion -/

/-- If `A → Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` is bijective and `I = (x,z)` is isomorphic as an `A`-module to
`Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))`, then `𝒪_U(-D)` is not a trivial invertible `𝒪_U`-module. -/
private theorem negativeTwist_not_trivial_of_bijective (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (hρ : Function.Bijective (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k))
    (hsect : Nonempty (coordinateIdeal k ≃ₗ[hypersurface k]
      (sectionsAsModuleFunctor k).obj (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)))) :
    ¬ Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsTrivial
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.presheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.ringCatIsSheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)) := by
  intro ⟨e⟩
  obtain ⟨eI⟩ := hsect
  let A := hypersurface k
  let U := (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum A).toScheme
  let ev := sectionsAsModuleFunctor k
  let eF := (ev.mapIso e).toLinearEquiv
  let ρlin : A →ₗ[A] (ev.obj (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit U.ringCatSheaf)) :=
    { toFun := sectionsAsModuleRingMap k
      map_add' := (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k).map_add
      map_smul' := fun a b => (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k).map_mul a b }
  let eA := LinearEquiv.ofBijective ρlin hρ
  let h : coordinateIdeal k ≃ₗ[A] A := eI.trans (eF.trans eA.symm)
  apply coordinateIdeal_not_principal k
  refine ⟨(h.symm 1).1, ?_⟩
  apply le_antisymm
  · intro a ha
    rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
    refine ⟨h ⟨a, ha⟩, ?_⟩
    have hh : h ⟨a, ha⟩ • h.symm 1 = ⟨a, ha⟩ := by
      apply h.injective
      simp
    have hv : h ⟨a, ha⟩ * (h.symm 1).1 = a := congrArg Subtype.val hh
    exact hv.symm.trans (mul_comm _ _)
  · exact Ideal.span_le.mpr (by simp)

/-- The sheaf `𝒪_U(-D) = ℐ_D` on the punctured spectrum `U` of `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)`, for
the divisor `D` cut out by `I = (x,z)`, is not a trivial invertible `𝒪_U`-module. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "nontrivial line bundle"]
public theorem negativeTwist_not_trivial' (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    ¬ Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsTrivial
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.presheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.ringCatIsSheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)) :=
  negativeTwist_not_trivial_of_bijective k (bijective_sectionsAsModuleRingMap k)
    (nonempty_coordinateIdeal_linearEquiv k)

/-- If `A → Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` is bijective and `I = (x,z)` is isomorphic as an `A`-module to
`Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))`, then `𝒪_U(-D)` is not a trivial invertible `𝒪_U`-module. -/
public theorem negativeTwist_not_trivial (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (hρ : Function.Bijective (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k))
    (hsect : Nonempty (coordinateIdeal k ≃ₗ[hypersurface k]
      (sectionsAsModuleFunctor k).obj (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)))) :
    ¬ Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsTrivial
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.presheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.ringCatIsSheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)) :=
  negativeTwist_not_trivial_of_bijective k hρ hsect

/-- If `D` is an effective Cartier divisor and `𝒪_U(-D)` is not trivial, then `Pic(U)` is
nontrivial. -/
private theorem not_subsingleton_picardGroup_of_not_trivial (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (cartierDivisor k))
    (h : ¬ Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsTrivial
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.presheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.ringCatIsSheaf
        (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k))) :
    ¬ Subsingleton
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.picardGroup := by
  intro hPic
  let U := (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme
  have := hD
  exact h ((U.picardClass_eq_zero_iff _
    (Stacks.Divisors.isTensorInvertible_negativeTwist (cartierDivisor k))).mp (hPic.allEq _ _))

/-- The Picard group `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.picardGroup` of the punctured spectrum
`U = Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` of `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is nontrivial. -/
@[stacks 0F2J "the conclusion: Pic(U) is nontrivial, at the same Scheme.picardGroup that \
Stacks 0F2I is stated at, so this is literally the negation of that proposition's conclusion \
for this A"]
public theorem picardGroup_not_subsingleton' (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    ¬ Subsingleton
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.picardGroup :=
  not_subsingleton_picardGroup_of_not_trivial k (isEffectiveCartierDivisor_cartierDivisor k)
    (negativeTwist_not_trivial' k)

/-- If `I = (x,z)` cuts out an effective Cartier divisor `D` on the punctured spectrum
`U = Spec A ∖ {𝔪}` of `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)`, `A → Γ(U, 𝒪_U)` is bijective and `I` is
isomorphic as an `A`-module to `Γ(U, 𝒪_U(-D))`, then the Picard group of `U` is nontrivial. -/
public theorem picardGroup_not_subsingleton (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (hD : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (cartierDivisor k))
    (hρ : Function.Bijective (sectionsAsModuleRingMap k))
    (hsect : Nonempty (coordinateIdeal k ≃ₗ[hypersurface k]
      (sectionsAsModuleFunctor k).obj (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (cartierDivisor k)))) :
    ¬ Subsingleton
      (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.picardGroup :=
  not_subsingleton_picardGroup_of_not_trivial k hD (negativeTwist_not_trivial k hρ hsect)

/-- *The dimension bound in [Stacks, Tag 0F2I] is sharp.*  For every
field `k` the ring `A = k⟦x,y,z,w⟧/(xy - zw)` is a Noetherian local complete intersection of
dimension exactly three — so it satisfies every hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0F2I] except
`dim A ≥ 4` — and the Picard group of its punctured spectrum is nontrivial. -/
@[stacks 0F2J]
public theorem dimension_bound_isSharp (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    IsNoetherianRing (hypersurface k) ∧ IsLocalRing (hypersurface k) ∧
      LocalCompleteIntersection.IsCompleteIntersectionRing (hypersurface k) ∧
      ringKrullDim (hypersurface k) = 3 ∧
      ¬ Subsingleton
        (Stacks.Divisors.puncturedSpectrum (hypersurface k)).toScheme.picardGroup :=
  ⟨hypersurface_isNoetherianRing k, hypersurface_isLocalRing k,
    hypersurface_isCompleteIntersectionRing k, hypersurface_krullDim k,
    picardGroup_not_subsingleton' k⟩


end Stacks.PuncturedSpectrumPicard.QuadricCone
